* Mac OS permisions fixes

## [1.0.3] - Update fixes
* Hide mac specific error in log. This error is not helpful so it has been hidden.

## [1.0.2] - Update fixes
* Change log display is now more readable.
* Fix for update mechanism now that the github is public.

## [1.0.1] - Update and tool tip fixes
* Small bug fix releated to tool tips getting stuck on page during network scan.
* Fix for update mechanism now that the github is public.

## [1.0.0] - Official Public Release
* Bumped version to 1.0.0 as the application has reached a stable point with most bugs fixed.
* The project has been officially made public for anyone to use.

## [0.15.4]
* Removed the Git dependency requirement within the setup scripts.
* Added a fallback option for the Speedtest mechanism.

## [0.15.3]
* Removed the Speedtest CLI Homebrew installation requirement on macOS.
* The application now downloads the Speedtest binary directly from the Speedtest website.

## [0.15.2]
* Fixed the update mechanism on Linux environments.

## [0.15.1]
* Fixed an issue with touch controls when accessing the dashboard from an iPad.
* The dashboard now remembers your active page upon refreshing.
* Fixed a bug in the network scan that caused unknown hostnames to display incorrectly.

## [0.15.0]
* Added a system tray icon that allows users to stop and restart the application.
* Introduced installer scripts for Windows, macOS, and Linux that fully handle the downloading and installation of requirements and code.

## [0.14.0]
* Fixed various server restart mechanisms.
* Unified the UI experience by ensuring all popups look and function consistently.
* Fixed an issue where comments were not available in certain sections.
* Fixed CSV exports to ensure comments are successfully exported.
* Tables can now be dynamically sorted via any column.

## [0.13.0]
* Added a Help section and tooltips for all functions.
* Added an Isolated Network Scan function, allowing for a new network scan that is not merged with previous data.
* Added the ability to merge network scan results and choose whether to use previous scan data for new scans.
* Various fixes and enhancements to network scanning.
* Added an option to restart and shut down the dashboard from Settings.
* Added an option to restart and shut down the OS when used as a standalone test device.
* Fixed file permissions and changed the logic regarding the setup script installing into the current folder.
* Updated installer scripts for Linux, macOS, and Windows.

## [0.12.5]
* Performance fixes for Windows and various quality of life improvements.

## [0.12.4]
* Wi-Fi scan fixes and UI tweaks.

## [0.12.3]
* Fixed a Wi-Fi scan bug on Windows that caused networks to be identified incorrectly.

## [0.12.2]
* Added an edit button to the network name on the network scan page.
* Fixed an issue with Wi-Fi network names.

## [0.12.1]
* UI tweaks.
* Added the ability to manually select the Wi-Fi adapter used for scanning.

## [0.12.0]
* Changed Wi-Fi and network device history to retain networks and devices even if the original scan is deleted.
* Fixed loading animations during network scanning.
* Added a mechanism to pause/sleep the page if it is inactive for more than 1 hour.

## [0.11.1 - 0.11.2]
* Testing releases.

## [0.11.0]
* Fixed various bugs and added failsafes should the application fail to start up correctly.
* Various UI fixes.
* You can now protect Speedtest, Ping, and DNS lookup results from the database clearing tool when removing data older than a certain time period.
* Prevented users from hiding all adapters (at least one must remain visible).
* Stopped the system from utilizing hidden adapters for any tasks.

## [0.10.0]
* Major fixes and improvements to resolve various issues.
* The dashboard can now be run on a Raspberry Pi.
* *Note: A Pi 4 is recommended due to performance and hardware limitations, though it supports a Pi 3.*
* Major rework of the network scanning engine, drastically improving responsiveness and functionality.

## [0.9.2]
* Minor UI bug fixes.
* Added a setting to disable the automatic browser launch on startup, useful for creating a dedicated headless device.
* Added basic user authentication (login credentials), highly useful when running from a dedicated device.
* Added the ability to change the active web server port.

## [0.9.1]
* Minor UI fixes and dashboard code cleanup (moved styles and scripts to separate files).
* Added the option to switch between Production and Development environments.

## [0.9.0]
* Introduced a new Device History page to look up historical data for devices found during network scans.
* Added an option to browse historical Wi-Fi networks.
* Fixed minor bugs with MAC address vendor lookups.
* Fixed search functionality and ensured selected items are remembered across page navigations.

## [0.8.1 - 0.8.3]
* Linux Wi-Fi speed fixes.

## [0.8.0]
* Enabled and fixed Wi-Fi scanning support for macOS.

## [0.7.14]
* Minor bug fixes.
* Fixed CSV export behavior when filtering results (the export button will now intelligently grab selected items, all items, or filtered items depending on context).

## [0.7.13]
* Fixed inconsistent network scans.
* Scans now accurately resolve and display Vendor IDs.
* Added a loading screen for the interface list on initial page load (prevents a blank screen).

## [0.7.12]
* Improved usability for touch-screen devices by adding a dedicated Touch Mode toggle.

## [0.7.11]
* Updated GitHub repository references in the setup script.

## [0.7.10]
* Speedtest bug fixes.

## [0.7.9]
* Network scan bug fixes.
* The scanning interface now explicitly labels 'This device' and the 'Router' in the list.
* If the router drops from the scan, it is automatically injected back into the list.
* Added Enter-key support for initiating Speedtests, DNS lookups, and Ping tests.
* Fixed formatting on the Speedtest table.

## [0.7.8]
* Boot time optimizations (reduced the time the app takes to start).
* File permissions are now only fixed during updates or initial GitHub cloning.
* Network scanning and Speedtest fixes.
* Added bulk deletion and bulk CSV export features for network and Wi-Fi scans.

## [0.7.7]
* Fixed the Windows launcher `.bat` file to resolve issues when starting offline.
* Fixed the setup script to resolve issues when starting offline.

## [0.7.6]
* Slightly updated the setup script to automatically launch the web browser when the server is ready.

## [0.7.5]
* Stability milestone: Tests show the application is now stable.
* Switched from the Flask debug server to the production Waitress WSGI server.
* Version tracking aligned across Setup (0.7.1), App (0.7.3), and Dashboard (0.7.1).
* *Note: No plans to update past this point unless bugs require fixing. Once deemed fully stable, the version will be bumped to 0.9.0 as the final beta version before 1.0.*

## [0.7.1 - 0.7.4]
* Minor fixes and update testing for Linux environments.

## [0.7.0]
* Major feature bump (Beta status).
* Fixed Speedtest logic to strictly use the active adapter unless an adapter is explicitly pinned.
* Various bug fixes.
* Local IP of the interface is now logged alongside Speedtest results.
* Added Database Import, Export, and Cleanup functionalities.
* Added a visual alert banner at the top of the page if an interface is pinned.

## [0.6.12 - 0.6.15]
* Update mechanism testing, update fixes, and file permission fixes.

## [0.6.11]
* Update mechanism fixes and minor bug fixes related to retrieving adapter hardware information.

## [0.6.10]
* Internal update test (no feature changes).

## [0.6.9]
* Fixed an issue with saving network scans as the same network when working across VLANs.
* Added visual loading indicators to the Network Scan page to indicate active scanning.
* Fixed Speedtest CLI downloads on Linux (added prompts to download manually from the Speedtest site if it fails).
* Additional fixes for the update mechanism.

## [0.6.8]
* Added the project logo and favicon to the dashboard.
* Dashboard version updated to 0.6.3.

## [0.6.7]
* Included launcher scripts for Windows, macOS, and Linux to ensure Python prerequisites are installed before executing the setup script.
* *Note: Update mechanism in the dashboard is still broken; deleting the app.py script will force a fresh download of the latest version.*

## [0.6.5 - 0.6.6]
* Various system fixes to allow functions to work correctly on Linux distributions.
* Version sync: Setup (0.6.0), App (0.6.6), Dashboard (0.6.1).

## [0.6.4]
* Additional Linux compatibility fixes.
* App script updated to 0.6.3, Setup script updated to 0.6.0.

## [0.6.3]
* Changelog separated into its own dedicated file.
* App script updated to 0.6.2 to reflect the new file reference.

## [0.6.2]
* Minor fixes to the setup script for improved Linux support.
* Setup script updated to 0.5.1.

## [0.6.1]
* Fixed adapter checks to prevent crashes when the device has absolutely no active connection (offline).

## [0.6.0]
* Various functional fixes.
* Major overhaul of the Wi-Fi scanning engine.
* *Note: Wi-Fi scanning is not functional on macOS yet. Tested and functional on Windows.*
* Windows Wi-Fi scanning briefly disables and re-enables the adapter to force a fresh airwave check.
* Dashboard UI updated to support the new features.
* Setup scripts updated to automatically install prerequisites on first boot.
* Version sync: Code (0.6.0), Setup (0.5.0), HTML Dashboard (0.6.0).

## [0.5.0]
* Various fixes and changes.
* Setup script now automatically clones the latest version from GitHub on its first run.
* Main app script updated to ensure general stability.
* Dashboard visuals updated.
* CSV exports are now fully functional.
* Removed various duplicated functions (Wi-Fi scanning tool still in development).

## [0.3.1]
* Fixed missing codebase references relating to the Speedtest tools.

## [0.3.0]
* Added the ability to save network scans and assign custom names to devices.
* Introduced the DNS Lookup and Ping tools.
* Dashboard updated to accommodate these new features.
* Setup script version remains 0.1.0; Main app script updated to 0.3.0.

## [0.2.0]
